    "hundred_pct_over_v8_head_s": -0.2,
    "hundred_pct_reasoning": "section 41.4 fitted B(K) = a + b/K to the member churn and section 44 read K = 5 -> 10 at +0.02250. Under that law K = 1 -> 10 is b(1 - 1/10) against b(1/5 - 1/10), a factor of 9, so one member should sit about 0.20 s below the bag",
    "monotone_in_rows": true,
    "reading_the_slope_is_fitted_to": "increment over the 100 % member",
    "refutes_it": "k's interval crossing zero kills the sample lever at this size; any subsampled level positive and clear over the 100 % member means the K = 1 churn dominates and nothing is extrapolated; the frac = 1.0 check missing its tolerance means no level is read at all",
    "registered_in": "RESULTS.md section 47.15, commit f714c16, before this file existed",
    "slope_k_band_s": [
      0.05,
      0.6
    ],
    "slope_k_board_s_per_nat": 0.25,
    "slope_k_reasoning": "two arguments point opposite ways and both are recorded: ABOVE 0.1912 because a down-weighted row still enters every split statistic and a deleted one does not; BELOW 0.1912 because the control's weights are a permutation and distort composition just as violently, so part of its -0.10998 is section 47.11's -0.14163 placement effect being charged to rows",
    "what_it_cannot_do": "subsampling the same two months is not the experiment of adding nine new ones. Section 47.6 measured clock coverage moving by tens of points between months, so the marginal new row need not be worth the marginal deleted one -- in EITHER direction"
  },
